WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:03.220
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.792
- I, uh, often do look at a
pile of stuff at work

00:00:05.792 --> 00:00:08.163
and think: “Maybe I should
stick that on my face.”

00:00:08.163 --> 00:00:09.758
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.758 --> 00:00:13.736
The Bob Bugs Project started
with just my Instagram account,

00:00:13.736 --> 00:00:17.530
and I started using it for an art diary.

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.034
I got an idea.

00:00:19.034 --> 00:00:22.367
Every day I disguise myself in some way.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.313
Day 363.

00:00:25.563 --> 00:00:28.157
Now for a creative breakthrough.

00:00:28.157 --> 00:00:31.074
(glass shattering)

00:00:34.568 --> 00:00:36.217
My name is Michael Gump.

00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:38.756
I am an art director and a prop master

00:00:38.756 --> 00:00:40.574
for crazy TV shows,

00:00:40.574 --> 00:00:43.374
and I'm also known as Bob Bugs.

00:00:43.374 --> 00:00:45.374
The Master of Disguise Project

00:00:45.374 --> 00:00:48.452
is partly to build creative strength

00:00:48.452 --> 00:00:52.264
or maybe to exorcise creative demons

00:00:52.264 --> 00:00:54.364
in a way that's not just at my job

00:00:54.364 --> 00:00:57.031
but also for my own evil wishes.

00:00:57.917 --> 00:00:58.820
You look at the picture,

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:00.860
it maybe seems like it
took a million years.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:02.979
I'm usually like, "I gotta get this done.

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:03.812
I gotta get to bed."

00:01:03.812 --> 00:01:07.105
So, I just get my stuff
and then set it all up

00:01:07.105 --> 00:01:08.419
and then.

00:01:08.419 --> 00:01:10.680
I usually, like, you know, start with this area

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.374
and then work my way out

00:01:12.374 --> 00:01:14.291
and then it'll be like.

00:01:18.539 --> 00:01:20.023
People ask me all the time like:

00:01:20.023 --> 00:01:24.369
“How many people do you
have to help you with that?”

00:01:24.369 --> 00:01:25.652
Usually nobody.

00:01:25.652 --> 00:01:27.034
- [Interviewer] Does it hurt?

00:01:27.034 --> 00:01:28.318
- One that stands out in my mind

00:01:28.318 --> 00:01:29.635
was kind of like what am I doing?

00:01:29.635 --> 00:01:31.437
I was putting clothespins on my face,

00:01:31.437 --> 00:01:33.270
and so I started sticking them on there

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:35.634
and then I kind of panicked a little bit

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:36.467
and I took them all off

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.722
and I was like, "Okay."

00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:40.375
And then I was like, "Okay,
this is gonna be fine."

00:01:40.375 --> 00:01:41.992
And then I put them all back on.

00:01:41.992 --> 00:01:44.152
You get used to discomfort pretty fast,

00:01:44.152 --> 00:01:46.193
but I'm concerned

00:01:46.193 --> 00:01:49.860
that it's definitely not
that good for my skin.

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:51.272
- [Interviewer] Do you have a favorite?

00:01:51.272 --> 00:01:52.949
- I do have a special place in my heart

00:01:52.949 --> 00:01:55.635
for that one that's like a green Mr. T

00:01:55.635 --> 00:01:57.533
because I just think it's funny,

00:01:57.533 --> 00:01:59.783
like Mr. Green T I call it.

00:02:01.717 --> 00:02:05.732
It's been a kind of exhausting
process in some ways.

00:02:05.732 --> 00:02:09.899
I usually only get like maybe
three hours of sleep a night.

00:02:13.939 --> 00:02:15.170
The discovery of the project

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:16.489
and part of the point of the project

00:02:16.489 --> 00:02:19.769
is that you don't always know what's good.

00:02:19.769 --> 00:02:22.431
So on the days that I really feel tired

00:02:22.431 --> 00:02:23.729
and I don't really want to do it,

00:02:23.729 --> 00:02:25.348
I don't really have a good idea,

00:02:25.348 --> 00:02:28.987
sometimes those projects come out better

00:02:28.987 --> 00:02:31.436
than the ones that I'm
really excited about.

00:02:31.436 --> 00:02:32.767
What's next?

00:02:32.767 --> 00:02:35.017
We'll have to wait and see.

